the operand-side padded window with the reversed kernel is the padded transposed convolution: true
the result-side unpadded window's extent is n + K - 1: true
the result-side unpadded window is the full transposed convolution: true
a result-side stride-only axis builds and runs: true
binary (the reported spec): result-side padded window `i=+k` in einsum spec "s, i; k => s, i=+k" is not supported: a padded (=+) window on the result is a padded transposed convolution, which OCANNL does not implement in one step. Build it in two: the full transposed convolution, with the result-side window unpadded (<+; its result extent is stride*(n-1) + the dilated kernel extent for an operand extent n), then a crop of `padding` cells at its start and `padding - output_padding` at its end (PyTorch's ConvTranspose arguments), written as a slice of a concatenated axis: "s, p^o^q => s, o" with the components p = padding and q = padding - output_padding captured and set (Shape.set_dim), or written as integer components ("s, 2^o^1 => s, o"); when output_padding > padding, slice only the start and pad the end with the output_padding - padding extra zero cells by a replacement ("s, a => s, a^r"); see docs/syntax_extensions.md. With stride 1, dilation 1 and an odd kernel size, the padded window on an operand with the kernel reversed (e.g. "s, o=+k; k => s, o") is the same map in one step.
binary (the reported spec): refused at construction, naming the result-side padded window i=+k: true
binary, strided and dilated: refused at construction, naming the result-side padded window 2*i=+2*k: true
unary: refused at construction, naming the result-side padded window i=+k: true
ternary: refused at construction, naming the result-side padded window i=+k: true
block: refused at construction, naming the result-side padded window s=+k: true
batch axis: refused at construction, naming the result-side padded window b=+k: true
input axis: refused at construction, naming the result-side padded window i=+k: true
axis before a row variable: refused at construction, naming the result-side padded window i=+k: true
legacy + with use_padding = true: refused at construction, naming the result-side padded window i=+k: true
%cd ~logic: refused at construction, naming the result-side padded window i=+k: true
